  "broadcast": {
   "src": "img/pov/stuntcar-broadcast.jpg",
   "w": 1280,
   "h": 720,
   "label": "Broadcast · same instant"
  },
  "details": [
   "Camera: one driver's-eye camera bolted to the car body (left seat, 1.15 m above the floor at rest), looking forward through the windshield, 320 × 240 pixels, 90° wide. It turns with the car in roll, pitch and yaw. A picture is taken when the program asks for it and arrives 20 ms later, stamped with its step.",
   "Car estimate: position, velocity, attitude and turn rates from the car's own navigation unit, with small noise and 10 ms old.",
   "Car state: the four wheels, the air left in each tank, the manifold pressures (real gauges with bias and noise), and the command in force.",
   "Referee: run number, practice or scored, run time, how the run ended, jumps landed, and each run's result: clearance, peak load, landing, difficulty, execution and points.",
   "Command: ten valve openings from 0 to 1 (four rear main jets, four corner jets pointing down, two front yaw jets; valves follow 20-25 ms late), torque for the two rear-wheel motors, brakes from 0 to 1, front-wheel steering, and how long to hold it (0.01 to 1 s). After that the valves close and the brakes go on.",
   "Timing: a control step every 10 ms; the world runs at real speed and never waits; a command acts at the next step, one in flight at a time.",
   "The car: one fill of compressed air (690 bar) per run is all the thrust there is; the car is held to the real vehicle's limits.",
   "A run: one jump off the flat floor over a row of parked vehicles into an 8 m corridor. Points = difficulty × execution, measured from the car's motion in the air: any rotation counts, more turns, reversals and axis changes score more, and a clean, straight, soft landing keeps the execution.",
   "A run scores nothing if the car touches anything, does not clear the row, lands too hard or crooked, tips over or leaves the corridor.",
   "The event: 2 practice runs, then 3 scored runs; the best two jumps of different tricks count. The world freezes after each run for a review of up to 5 minutes.",
   "Before the event: 30 minutes of preparation with a full practice copy of the course. No GPU."
  ]
